{"name":"Twice Shy","hex":"#ca999e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"twice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Two times.","Doubled in quantity, intensity, or degree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twice"},{"term":"shy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tachawit. The native name for the Shawiya language."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Easily frightened; timid.","Reserved; disinclined to familiar approach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dick Francis","blocks":[{"text":"Richard Stanley Francis was a British steeplechase jockey and crime writer whose novels centre on horse racing in England."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/29/Dick_Francis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dick_Francis"},{"title":"Interactive fiction","blocks":[{"text":"Interactive fiction (IF) is software simulating environments in which players use text commands to control characters and influence the environment. Works in this form can be understood as literary narratives, either in the form of interactive narratives or interactive narrations. These works can also be understood as a form of video game, either in the form of an adventure game or role-playing game. In common usage, the term refers to text adventures, a type of adventure game where the entire interface can be \"text-only\", however, graphical text adventure games, where the text is accompanied by graphics still fall under the text adventure category if the main way to interact with the game is by typing text. Some users of the term distinguish between interactive fiction, known as \"puzzle-free\", that focuses on narrative, and \"text adventures\" that focus on puzzles."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interactive_fiction"},{"title":"Twice","blocks":[{"text":"Twice is a South Korean girl group formed by JYP Entertainment. The group is composed of nine members: Nayeon, Jeongyeon, Momo, Sana, Jihyo, Mina, Dahyun, Chaeyoung, and Tzuyu. They are recognized as one of the best-selling girl groups of all time and are widely regarded as one of K-pop's most influential acts. Twice have been dubbed \"The Nation's Girl Group\" in their home country and are credited for their role in leading the re-emergence of girl groups in the Korean Wave. Initially known for their bright and youthful image, the group has since evolved to explore an array of sounds and concepts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Twice_260618.jpg/330px-Twice_260618.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twice"},{"title":"Shyness","blocks":[{"text":"Shyness is a psychological trait characterized by social inhibition and apprehension in response to new social environments or perceived social judgement. It is frequently associated with social avoidance. Although shyness can be an attribute of people who have low self-esteem, the trait is often defined by a concern regarding the negative evaluation of others, such as mocking or rejection. While shyness is considered a normal personality variant, it is distinct from clinical conditions such as social anxiety disorder, which involves impairment in daily functioning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/20220801_Introversion_-_Shyness_-_Social_anxiety_disorder_-_comparative_chart.svg/330px-20220801_Introversion_-_Shyness_-_Social_anxiety_disorder_-_comparative_chart.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shyness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Zork_I_screenshot_video_game_Gargoyle_interpreter_on_Ubuntu_Linux.png/250px-Zork_I_screenshot_video_game_Gargoyle_interpreter_on_Ubuntu_Linux.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/32/Zork_I_screenshot_video_game_Gargoyle_interpreter_on_Ubuntu_Linux.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/32/Zork_I_screenshot_video_game_Gargoyle_interpreter_on_Ubuntu_Linux.png/250px-Zork_I_screenshot_video_game_Gargoyle_interpreter_on_Ubuntu_Linux.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zork I is one of the first interactive fiction games, as well as being one of the first commercially sold.  It is one of the most famous interactive fiction games. Here it is portrayed running on Gargoyle, a modern interpreter.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZork_I_screenshot_video_game_Gargoyle_interpreter_on_Ubuntu_Linux.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Park_Jin-young_%28Founder_of_JYP_Entertainment%29_in_February_2011_from_acrofan.jpg/500px-Park_Jin-young_%28Founder_of_JYP_Entertainment%29_in_February_2011_from_acrofan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Park_Jin-young_%28Founder_of_JYP_Entertainment%29_in_February_2011_from_acrofan.jpg/500px-Park_Jin-young_%28Founder_of_JYP_Entertainment%29_in_February_2011_from_acrofan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"JYPE founder J. Y. Park is credited with creating the group's name","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APark_Jin-young_(Founder_of_JYP_Entertainment)_in_February_2011_from_acrofan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Twice_performing_at_SAC_2016_02_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Twice_performing_at_SAC_2016_02_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb